  "answer_text": "The \"thin PFG\" shirts made by Columbia (**PFG** stands for **Performance Fishing Gear**) are known by a few specific model names depending on their style:\n\n### 1. The Thin Button-Down Style (Woven)\nIf you are looking for the classic button-up collar shirt with pockets, it is likely one of these two:\n* **The Columbia PFG Tamiami (or Tamiami II):** This is Columbia\u2019s **lightest and thinnest** button-down fishing shirt. It is made from an ultra-thin, silky, 100% polyester ripstop fabric. It is highly breathable, wicks sweat, and feels almost weightless.\n* **The Columbia PFG Bahama (or Bahama II):** This is another incredibly popular lightweight button-down, though it is slightly stiffer and thicker than the Tamiami because it is made of a structured \"Tactel\" nylon rather than polyester. \n\n### 2. The Thin T-Shirt / Hoodie Style (Knit Sun Shirts)\nIf you are looking for the silky, stretchy, long-sleeve performance shirts (often with a hood) designed to block the sun, they are called:\n* **The Columbia PFG Terminal Tackle:** This is the highly popular, ultra-thin, silky long-sleeve tech tee (available as a crew neck or a hoodie). It is made of lightweight, quick-drying polyester with UPF 50 sun protection. \n* **The Columbia PFG Tidal Tee:** This is the women's version of the Terminal Tackle, featuring the same ultra-thin, silky, sun-protecting fabric.\n\n**General Category Name:** Broadly, these lightweight, thin garments are referred to in the outdoor industry as **sun shirts**, **solar hoodies**, or **UPF protection shirts**.",
